==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{unc|ru}}. {{w|Max Vasmer|Vasmer}} hypothesizes the existence of an earlier form, {{inh|ru|orv|*бубага}}, from which {{m|ru|бума́га}} formed through dissimilation, or perhaps a {{back-formation|ru|бума́жный|nocap=1}}. Believed to be ultimately from {{der|ru|pal|pmbk'|t=cotton}} through the intermediary of some Mediterranean term for cotton wool and/or cloth (most probably {{der|ru|it|bambagia}}), since the first attestations of the root in the 15th and 16th centuries are mostly with a now obsolete sense, the only remnant of which in modern active vocabulary is {{l|ru|хлопчатобума́жный|t=made from cotton}}. Paper was first imported into Russia from Italian states and the Byzantine Empire in the 14th century.

